          [{ "text": "3 3 2 x x x", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "G2 C3 E3", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "2–3" }]
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Chapter 2 already made the case for "
        },
        {
          "text": "choosing a set",
          "link": { "kind": "article", "slug": "triad-choosing-a-set" }
        },
        {
          "text": " by register and by what else is sounding. What's new here is that the choice isn't made once for the whole song. A verse played low on strings 3-4-5 and a chorus played up on strings 1-2-3 is the same chords and the same fingering logic, just more energy — and it costs nothing but a set."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here's the fact that makes crossing cheap, and it's new: take a progression that uses the same inversions on every set, and each string moves by exactly the same number of frets, no matter which set you're on."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "header": [
        [{ "text": "Set" }],
        [{ "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] }],
        [{ "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] }],
        [{ "text": "Am", "marks": ["code"] }],
        [{ "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] }],
        [{ "text": "Frets" }]
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          [{ "text": "1-2-3" }],
          [{ "text": "x x x 5 5 3", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "x x x 4 3 3", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "x x x 5 5 5", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "x x x 5 6 5", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "3–6" }]
        ],
        [
          [{ "text": "2-3-4" }],
          [{ "text": "x x 10 9 8 x", "marks": ["code"] }],
          [{ "text": "x x 9 7 8 x", "marks": ["code"] }],
