    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The movement from chord to chord is the same row on all four sets, low string first: "
        },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " → " },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " is " },
        { "text": "−1 −2 0", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": "; " },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " → " },
        { "text": "Am", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " is " },
        { "text": "+1 +2 +2", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": "; " },
        { "text": "Am", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " → " },
        { "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " is " },
        { "text": "0 +1 0", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": "; " },
        { "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " → " },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " is " },
        { "text": "0 −1 −2", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ". The reason is exact, not a coincidence: the lift across the " },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " → " },
        { "text": "B", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " break belongs to the " },
        { "text": "set", "marks": ["italic"] },
        {
          "text": ", and it applies to both chords in a change equally, so it cancels the moment you subtract one grip from the next. "
        },
        { "text": "The grips change from set to set. The moves don't.", "marks": ["bold"] },
        {
          "text": " There is one limit on that: it holds only while the whole run stays inside one octave copy of the shapes — a grip forced up an octave to stay on the neck breaks the pattern."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That progression is "
        },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ", " },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ", " },
        { "text": "Am", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ", " },
        { "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " — in other words " },
        { "text": "I V vi IV", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ", using " },
        {
          "text": "the numbers from harmonising the scale",
          "link": { "kind": "article", "slug": "triad-harmonising-the-major-scale" }
        },
        { "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here's a worked crossing: two bars, "
        },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " then " },
        { "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ", then " },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " then " },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": ". Play " },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " and " },
        { "text": "F", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " low on strings 3-4-5, then jump to " },
        { "text": "G", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " and " },
        { "text": "C", "marks": ["code"] },
        { "text": " up on strings 1-2-3." }
      ]
